{"event_type":"review","id":"1acfd79acfa68f8b4685036a55563ca0f46fbd48139a99831d0d9b6ea00c9506","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T03:48:46Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4f72a874202040c99afb2ed5c9b353a4364c2684a7aefbe36afb086f5eea6189","sha256":"4f72a874202040c99afb2ed5c9b353a4364c2684a7aefbe36afb086f5eea6189"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1089cc67e7cc46723fe89aa486c6f3c16076356882da1e572753b8678e9ab671","sha256":"1089cc67e7cc46723fe89aa486c6f3c16076356882da1e572753b8678e9ab671"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6d69215ee0b52e5a8e9c24ca9fdbda84923f99bbc2a3605a79a0d5dcb17fed39","sha256":"6d69215ee0b52e5a8e9c24ca9fdbda84923f99bbc2a3605a79a0d5dcb17fed39"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/eb0491522c9e5d603ed7b65b8077d7afd34f69c0928d72728ac37226f4204b41","sha256":"eb0491522c9e5d603ed7b65b8077d7afd34f69c0928d72728ac37226f4204b41"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4ee17996ab3522f3fe5652d260940cd3a07fb2a358f79b30ea8e7ed22f539b85","sha256":"4ee17996ab3522f3fe5652d260940cd3a07fb2a358f79b30ea8e7ed22f539b85"}],"attempt_id":"f2ae1ba86b973b956e7582c5cee4445a645d21f4452cff17366e428fb67e300c:0:1","base":"0382c67fb74d5f29af7ebf4eb998947c96f8afdc","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"fb09ced56678f6cb9fe8288ea0548f13e01712fe","body":"**Reject metadata whose serialized size exceeds the reader's 16384-byte limit.**\n\n`writeMetadata` validates the schema but never checks the size of the document it writes. `readSlotMetadata` rejects any file over 16384 bytes. A valid bound state can exceed that limit. `JSON.stringify` expands control characters and quotes in `checkoutPath` and `checkoutGitDir`, so long resolved paths made of such characters can serialize past the limit. The writer then persists the file, and every later `readMetadata` or `assertReusable` call on that slot throws `Oversized slot metadata` until the file is removed.\n\nUnknown fields also survive validation and are written unchanged. A caller that bypasses the `SlotMetadata` type can add a field such as `note: 'x'.repeat(16384)` to trigger the same failure.\n\nSerialize once, measure the UTF-8 byte length including the newline, and reject before the temporary file is created. The existing document then stays unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+      const text = `${JSON.stringify(canonical)}\\n`;\n+      if (Buffer.byteLength(text, 'utf8') > 16_384) throw new Error('Oversized slot metadata');\n       const temporary = `${metadataPath}.${randomUUID()}.tmp`;\n       const output = await open(temporary, 'wx', 0o600);\n       try {\n-        await output.writeFile(`${JSON.stringify(canonical)}\\n`);\n+        await output.writeFile(text);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"4691ffad1c1d400b4de164d77d54ade2d736b5c9b1c3ed0d1e32fcc16f2caf21","intervals":[[212,212]],"path":"src/adapters/lock/slotLock.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject metadata whose serialized size exceeds the reader's 16384-byte limit."}],"head":"831d21c2f3a907fb78ed1cf1da5a3585ab9e2916","head_tree":"1ecd116c4ac33bbae984033dfd03894947e6454f","input_scope":[{"blob":"1d0b75d12097cf7a1b0b945ffc6b0e259731906f","intervals":[[1,5]],"path":"src/adapters/lock/fs-ext.d.ts"},{"blob":"fb09ced56678f6cb9fe8288ea0548f13e01712fe","intervals":[[1,232]],"path":"src/adapters/lock/slotLock.ts"}],"job_id":"f2ae1ba86b973b956e7582c5cee4445a645d21f4452cff17366e428fb67e300c:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"1d0b75d12097cf7a1b0b945ffc6b0e259731906f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/lock/fs-ext.d.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"fb09ced56678f6cb9fe8288ea0548f13e01712fe","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/lock/slotLock.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"1d0b75d12097cf7a1b0b945ffc6b0e259731906f","intervals":[[1,5]],"path":"src/adapters/lock/fs-ext.d.ts"},{"blob":"fb09ced56678f6cb9fe8288ea0548f13e01712fe","intervals":[[25,25],[30,32],[46,46],[125,125]],"path":"src/adapters/lock/slotLock.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"1d0b75d12097cf7a1b0b945ffc6b0e259731906f","intervals":[[1,5]],"path":"src/adapters/lock/fs-ext.d.ts"},{"blob":"fb09ced56678f6cb9fe8288ea0548f13e01712fe","intervals":[[25,25],[30,32],[46,46],[125,125]],"path":"src/adapters/lock/slotLock.ts"}],"scope_digest":"9460214076a03745b6de1c2cecf508fafc5227bda52abb85f939c885f69c06d0","source":{"authenticated":true,"id":"backfill-f2ae1ba86b973b956e7582c5cee4445a645d21f4452cff17366e428fb67e300c-g0-20261117T034349Z","producer":"crq-runner-app","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","type":"crq-run"},"subject_id":"f2ae1ba86b973b956e7582c5cee4445a645d21f4452cff17366e428fb67e300c","target":"b49018293f5b97dee705fc1fe8c83dfc40903162","target_tree":"1ecd116c4ac33bbae984033dfd03894947e6454f"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit:crq-runner-app:backfill-f2ae1ba86b973b956e7582c5cee4445a645d21f4452cff17366e428fb67e300c-g0-20261117T034349Z"}